{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>For not</b> — [the word] ישרת [i.e. the verse] stands for itself, and what follows it with it, like: \"Let Reuben live and not die, and let not his men be few\" and \"nor have I learned wisdom.\" The sense: the hope of the poor will not perish forever."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:45.816874163Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}